course: dictionary
lesson: 2744
title: A word about fairness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some people start life with fewer chances than others. A word for this is disadvantaged. It means having fewer chances than other people because of being poor, ill, or having a hard home life. The official phrase «economically disadvantaged» means poor.
explain: Use the words around it to work out the meaning. A disadvantaged background is a start in life with fewer chances. Schools in disadvantaged areas are schools in places where many families have less money or fewer chances. Ask yourself what would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Disadvantaged is a formal, polite word. You will meet it in the news and in social studies. It describes a situation, not a person's worth or character.
fact: Disadvantaged means having fewer chances than other people.
fact: Chances can be lost because of being poor, being ill, or having a hard home life.
fact: «Economically disadvantaged» is an official phrase that means poor.
fact: The disadvantaged means people who are disadvantaged, as a group. This use is formal.
fact: Phrases you may meet are disadvantaged background, disadvantaged groups, and socially disadvantaged.
exercise: What does disadvantaged mean? | Having more money than everyone else | *Having fewer chances than other people | Being very tall for your age | Always winning games
exercise: The official phrase «economically disadvantaged» means what? | *Poor | Clever | Very old | Ill with a cold
exercise: In «The disadvantaged need more help from the school», what does the disadvantaged mean? | A kind of school bus | The weather report | *People who are disadvantaged, as a group | A single teacher
test: Which is a reason someone may be disadvantaged? | Liking maths | Having a birthday in June | Living near the sea | *Having a hard home life
test: A disadvantaged background means what? | A huge garden | A cheap dinner | *A start in life with fewer chances | A background painting in art class
exam: Which sentence uses disadvantaged correctly? | Disadvantaged means very tall | The disadvantaged is a sort of dinner | Disadvantaged is the colour of a clear sky | *Schools in disadvantaged areas may need extra support
